[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112935,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 25,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Sinonasal ameloblastoma (SA) is a benign but locally aggressive extragnathic sinonasal tract epithelial odontogenic neoplasm composed of ameloblast-like cells and stellate reticulum.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:24:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112936,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 25,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9310/0 Ameloblastoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:24:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112937,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 25,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E83.0 &amp; XH1SV4 Benign osteogenic tumours of bone or articular cartilage of skull or face &amp; Ameloblastoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:24:27"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112938,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 25,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:24:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112939,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 25,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:24:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112940,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 25,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SA affects the nasal cavity (septum, lateral wall), paranasal sinuses, or both {9477098; 23243540}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:24:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112941,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 25,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients commonly present with nasal obstruction and/or epistaxis {9477098}. With tumour progression, extension into the nasal vestibule {3927244; 22507424} or orbitofacial deformity may develop {3927244; 9477098}.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>Imaging studies reveal a solid rather than multicystic appearance, with remodelled and/or destroyed sinus bony walls {22507424}. Radiographic evidence of an intraosseous maxillary alveolar bone component precludes a diagnosis of SA {9477098}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:24:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112942,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 25,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SA is very rare, with a strong male predilection. Patients are adults in their sixth to seventh decade of life, notably older than those with its gnathic counterparts {9477098; 29846904}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:24:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112943,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 25,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:24:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112944,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 25,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Although not studied in sinonasal tract tumours, <em>BRAF</em> activating mutations are most common in jaw tumours, followed by mutually exclusive RAS mutations {24374844; 24859340; 24993163; 30216733}, with <em>SMO</em> mutation being a common co-occurring mutation {24859340; 24993163}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:24:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112945,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 25,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cut surface is solid with limited cystic change {9477098; 29846904}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:24:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112946,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 25,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SA is a basaloid epithelial neoplasm commonly arranged in a plexiform or follicular pattern, with a loosely arranged stellate reticulum&ndash;like component centrally. Peripheral cells palisade with reverse polarity and subnuclear vacuolization. Direct surface epithelial continuity may be identified {9477098}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The differential diagnosis includes salivary gland neoplasms, skin basal cell carcinoma, and basaloid squamous cell carcinoma. Craniopharyngioma is separable with clinicoradiographic correlation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:24:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112947,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 25,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "<p>Hypercellular smears show tissue fragments of small basaloid cells with hyperchromatic round nuclei and peripheral palisading, and distinct larger cells with more open chromatin. There may be occasional stromal fragments with spindle cells with elongated nuclei and abundant clear cytoplasm {9250285}. Keratin and cholesterol crystals are not seen {32841532}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-09T11:59:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112948,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 25,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "<p>Not clinically relevant</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-09T12:00:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112949,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 25,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> sinonasal location; radiographic exclusion of jaw origin; ameloblastic-type epithelium with central stellate reticulum&ndash;like material.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:24:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112950,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 25,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:24:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112951,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 25,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Morbidity depends on tumour size and sites of tumour extension. Local recurrences may occur, but no distant metastases are reported {9477098}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:24:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]